DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     yyppxxffrr is the utility in YP that transfers maps to the local host.

     Since the YP master transfers a map when it has changed, a YP slave
     should check for missed maps regularly.  This can be done via an entry in
     crontab(5).  The scripts _y_p_x_f_r___1_p_e_r_h_o_u_r, _y_p_x_f_r___2_p_e_r_d_a_y and _y_p_x_f_r___1_p_e_r_d_a_y
     could be used for that.

     The options are as follows:

     --CC _t_i_d _p_r_o_g _i_p_a_d_d _p_o_r_t
             This option is only used by ypserv.  This is to open communica‐
             tion with a yppush on another host.

     --cc      Don't send a "Clear current map" to local ypserv process.  Useful
             if ypserv isn't running locally to avoid timeout message.

     --dd _d_o_m_a_i_n
             Don't use default domain, use the specified domain.

     --ff      Force map transfer, even if version of master is older than local
             copy.

     --hh _h_o_s_t
             Get map from host instead of the maps master host.

     --ss _d_o_m_a_i_n
             Specify a source domain other than the target domain.

